//? Title: PBKDF2: actual HMAC chains and block XORs
//? Subtitle: Canonical C++ producers, original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
For each output block, U1 hashes salt followed by the one-based big-endian block
index. Later U values hash the preceding32-byte U; their XOR forms that output
block. The requested prefix is returned. The exact producing HMAC calls are
counted, including every partial output block. Distinct salts alter these
fixtures but cannot make a finite hash collision-free or add password entropy.
Public tiny iteration counts are educational fixtures, not deployment settings.
[RFC8018 section5.2|https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8018#section-5.2] defines
the construction. No external dataset is needed.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

For each output block, U1 hashes salt followed by the one-based big-endian block
index. Later U values hash the preceding32-byte U; their XOR forms that output
block. The requested prefix is returned. The exact producing HMAC calls are
counted, including every partial output block. Distinct salts alter these
fixtures but cannot make a finite hash collision-free or add password entropy.
Public tiny iteration counts are educational fixtures, not deployment settings.
[RFC8018 section5.2|https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8018#section-5.2] defines
the construction. No external dataset is needed.

$$ U_1=\operatorname{HMAC}(P,S\Vert\operatorname{INT32BE}(i)),\quad U_j=\operatorname{HMAC}(P,U_{j-1}),\quad T_i=\bigoplus_{j=1}^{c}U_j. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native diagram use the same producing run. Captured records own
their values; the report does not reconstruct the algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pbkdf2_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::pbkdf2_hmac_sha256_trace("password", "salt", 2, 32);
    std::print("| block | round | actual U | actual running XOR |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | `{}` | `{}` |\n", r.block, r.round,
                   dm::algorithms::to_hex(r.u),
                   dm::algorithms::to_hex(r.accumulator));
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first block\n{} rounds", t.steps.size()));
    d.node("n1", {8, 0}, std::format("Actual HMAC calls\n{}", t.hmac_calls));
    d.node("n2", {16, 0},
           std::format("Actual key prefix\n{} bytes", t.key.size()));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pbkdf2_tiny.svg");
}
```
